    "q-143485": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143485",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{148}$ be a random sample of size $n=148$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu =98$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma =74.$ Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $95.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ | $\\,0.2810\\,$ | $\\,0.2776\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ | $\\,0.3156\\,$ | $\\,0.3121\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nn=148,\\,\\mu =98,\\,\\sigma =74.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(98,\\frac{{74}^{2}}{148}) \\\\  & ∼N(98,37).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}>95).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>95) & =P(Z>\\frac{95-98}{\\sqrt{37}}) \\\\  & =P(Z>-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{37}}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>-0.49)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the complement of the normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>-0.49) & =1-P(Z<-0.49) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.49).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.49)=0.3121.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>95) & =1-Φ(-0.49) \\\\  & =1-0.3121 \\\\  & =0.6879.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
