    "q-143484": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143484",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{98}$ be a random sample of size $n=98$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu =180$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma =70.$ Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is greater than $182.$\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.5279\\,$ | $\\,0.5319\\,$ | $\\,0.5359\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5675\\,$ | $\\,0.5714\\,$ | $\\,0.5753\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose that ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a random sample of size $n$ from a population with a population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ The central limit theorem (or CLT) states that for sufficiently large $n,$ the distribution of the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ can be approximated as \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nn=98,\\,\\mu =180,\\,\\sigma =70.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the CLT, we have that the distribution of the sample mean can be approximated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X} & ∼N\\,(\\mu ,\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}) \\\\  & ∼N\\,(180,\\frac{{70}^{2}}{98}) \\\\  & ∼N(180,50).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to find $P(\\overset{―}{X}>182).$ So, we convert $\\overset{―}{X}$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>182) & =P(Z>\\frac{182-180}{\\sqrt{50}}) \\\\  & =P(Z>\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}) \\\\  & ≈P(Z>0.28)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the complement of the normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>0.28) & =1-P(Z<0.28) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.28).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.28)=0.6103.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\overset{―}{X}>182) & =1-Φ(0.28) \\\\  & =1-0.6103 \\\\  & =0.3897.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
